{
  "id": "https://m-lancini.github.io/frida-vocab/dictionary/personal-assistance",
  "type": "Concept",
  "prefLabel": {
    "en": "personal assistance"
  },
  "definition": {
    "en": "A form of support for people with disabilities that focuses on self-determination, in which the person receiving assistance decides how the assistance is organised and utilised. The goal is to enable people to lead as self-determined a life as possible and to participate in society on an equal footing."
  },
  "scopeNote": {
    "en": [
      "It involves supporting the person with a disability in performing daily activities, moving around, and participating in social and professional life, enabling the person with a disability to live independently. It provides support in everyday activities that the person cannot perform independently, such as dressing, personal care, leaving the house, getting around town, administering medication, shopping, maintaining relationships with friends, and performing professional work. A personal assistant is not a caregiver. They are a person who supports the person with a disability in their daily functioning, enabling them to lead an independent and active life. A personal assistant acts in accordance with the will of the person they support, respecting their independence and choices. The scope of their support is tailored to the individual needs of the person using the personal assistance service"
    ]
  },
  "notation": [
    "1.12"
  ],
  "broader": {
